[
  {
    "comment": "Fragility and seepage on Clayworks' own fired ware. This matters for the six Clayworks-exclusive colours (azure, crimson, green, orange, pink, snow): those are the only ware that actually reaches a clayworks:-domain fired block, because the blue/red/fire chain dries back into vanilla game: ware. Without this file, a player working in Clayworks colours would see none of rung 1 or rung 2.",
    "file": "clayworks:blocktypes/clay/bowl.json",
    "op": "addmerge",
    "path": "/behaviors",
    "value": [{ "name": "rudiments:Fragile" }, { "name": "rudiments:Seepage" }],
    "dependsOn": [{ "modid": "clayworks" }]
  },
  {
    "comment": "Their bowl and jug are the two Clayworks vessels with liquidContainerProps, so they are the two that can seep — and like vanilla they need the class swap, not just the behavior, because BlockLiquidContainerBase.OnHeldInteractStart does not call base on the fill/pour path.",
    "file": "clayworks:blocktypes/clay/bowl.json",
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/classByType/*-fired*",
    "value": "rudiments:BlockSeepingContainer",
    "dependsOn": [{ "modid": "clayworks" }]
  },
